<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <BrandHead
        title="Product decisions are the code — Fluxzero"
        description="See how everyday product features become simple code when Fluxzero handles the engineering underneath."
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/v4.css?v=20260905-1">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/technical-foundation.css?v=20260904-5">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/technical-foundation-next.css?v=20260910-11">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/product-code.css?v=20260912-34">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/marketing-shell.css?v=20260903-1">
</head>
<body class="v4-page cloud-proof-page cloud-proof-next-page product-code-page">
    <MarketingHeader active="how-it-works" />

    <main>
        <header class="cloud-proof-hero cloud-proof-next-hero product-code-hero">
            <span class="product-code-hero__sun" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell product-code-hero__layout">
                <div class="product-code-hero__copy">
                    <p class="cloud-proof-hero__back" data-reveal><a href="/how-it-works#behavior-title" data-browser-back><i class="bx bx-left-arrow-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i> Back</a></p>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__eyebrow" data-reveal>Product code</p>
                    <h1 data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">Product decisions<br><span>are the code.</span></h1>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-hero__lead" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">When the cloud handles the engineering underneath, a feature can be just its business rules and follow-up actions. These examples show what that leaves your agent to write.</p>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-hero__lead product-code-hero__context" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">You build in natural language. Fluxzero chose Java for the code underneath: a proven backend language that agents speak fluently. Your code remains easy to extend as your product grows.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </header>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="intent" aria-labelledby="intent-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">01 · Making changes</p>
                    <h2 id="intent-title">Only product logic.<br><span>Working at any scale.</span></h2>
                    <p>You decide how a feature should work. Fluxzero keeps its rules intact when many customers act at once. The same logic continues to work as usage grows, without engineering work for your agent.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--action" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="ReserveTicket.java" label="Command, rule, two changes" code={actionCode} />
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>State loads automatically</dt><dd>Fluxzero provides the product state and which customer is making the change.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Everything changes together</dt><dd>If something changes while the rule runs, Fluxzero runs it again before saving.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Many people, one safe result</dt><dd>Each decision is kept correct even when many customers act at once.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="domain-state" aria-labelledby="domain-state-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">02 · Keeping track</p>
                    <h2 id="domain-state-title">Your code describes the product.<br><span>Fluxzero keeps its history.</span></h2>
                    <p>Define the parts of your product and how they fit together. Fluxzero keeps the information up to date and preserves its history. Your app can use that history directly in its features.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--model" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <figure class="product-code-relation-map">
                        <div class="product-code-relation-map__grid">
                            <ProductCodePanel class="product-code-relation-map__code product-code-relation-map__code--show" title="Show.java" label="Root model" code={showModelCode} />
                            <div class="product-code-relation-map__level product-code-relation-map__level--show">
                                <span class="product-code-relation-map__link product-code-relation-map__link--show-ticket" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <strong class="product-code-relation-map__root">Show</strong>
                            </div>

                            <ProductCodePanel class="product-code-relation-map__code product-code-relation-map__code--tickets" title="Ticket.java" label="Child of Show" code={ticketModelCode} />
                            <div class="product-code-relation-map__level product-code-relation-map__level--tickets">
                                <span class="product-code-relation-map__link product-code-relation-map__link--ticket-up" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <span class="product-code-relation-map__link product-code-relation-map__link--ticket-down" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <ul class="product-code-relation-map__tickets" aria-label="Tickets connected to the show">
                                    <li><span>Ticket</span></li>
                                    <li class="is-reserved"><span>Ticket</span></li>
                                    <li><span>Ticket</span></li>
                                    <li class="is-reserved"><span>Ticket</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>

                            <ProductCodePanel class="product-code-relation-map__code product-code-relation-map__code--reservations" title="Reservation.java" label="Child of Ticket" code={reservationModelCode} />
                            <div class="product-code-relation-map__level product-code-relation-map__level--reservations">
                                <span class="product-code-relation-map__link product-code-relation-map__link--reservation-up" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <ul class="product-code-relation-map__reservations" aria-label="Reservations connected to tickets">
                                    <li aria-hidden="true"></li>
                                    <li>
                                        <span>Reservation<small>Paid</small></span>
                                    </li>
                                    <li aria-hidden="true"></li>
                                    <li>
                                        <span class="is-pending">Reservation<small>Pending</small></span>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>Keep track of everything</dt><dd>Fluxzero keeps track of every part of the product and how it relates to the rest.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Stored automatically</dt><dd>Fluxzero loads and saves the information without storage work in the application.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>History preserved</dt><dd>Fluxzero keeps every previous state of the product available.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="tests" aria-labelledby="tests-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">03 · Testing behavior</p>
                    <h2 id="tests-title">Know it works.<br><span>Before customers use it.</span></h2>
                    <p>Your agent tests that features keep working as you build. That includes the edge cases. Fluxzero runs the same product code and rules in tests as in production, so you can ship with confidence.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--test" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="ReserveTicketTest.java" label="Behavior test with JSON" code={testCode} />
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>Production behavior</dt><dd>Fluxzero runs the scenario through the same rules as the real application.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Real circumstances</dt><dd>Fluxzero supplies the person and moment described by the test.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Visible outcome</dt><dd>Fluxzero confirms success or the expected rejection without inspecting internals.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="search" aria-labelledby="search-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">04 · Finding information</p>
                    <h2 id="search-title">Your product data.<br><span>Search built in.</span></h2>
                    <p>Query your data from anywhere in your code. Use a dedicated query class to define what to fetch and who may access it. Fluxzero keeps your data and its relationships searchable as the product changes, without a separate search system to build or maintain.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--query" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="FindAvailableTickets.java" label="Query and search" code={searchCode} />
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>Search maintained automatically</dt><dd>Fluxzero updates the searchable data as your product changes.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Relationships already known</dt><dd>Fluxzero follows the connections in your product data to find what belongs together.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Work done in the cloud</dt><dd>Fluxzero filters and sorts the data. Your code receives the results it asked for.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="workflows" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">05 · Set a schedule</p>
                    <h2 id="workflows-title">Your product follows up.<br><span>Even after a restart.</span></h2>
                    <p>Scheduling is part of almost every application. Fluxzero makes it easy to schedule and test what should happen later. Scheduled work survives restarts and deployments, with your rules checked when it runs.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--stacked" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <div class="product-code-proof__code-stack">
                        <ProductCodePanel title="ReservationTimers.java" label="Start and cancel a deadline" code={timerCode} />
                        <ProductCodePanel title="ExpireReservation.java" label="Remove hold and release ticket" code={expiryCode} />
                    </div>
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>Scheduled work preserved</dt><dd>Fluxzero retains the action through application restarts and deployments.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Current rules checked</dt><dd>Fluxzero loads the latest data and checks whether the scheduled change is still allowed.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Cancellation handled</dt><dd>Your code names the follow-up to cancel. Fluxzero removes it from the schedule.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="durable-workflows" aria-labelledby="durable-workflows-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">06 · Run a workflow</p>
                    <h2 id="durable-workflows-title">Workflows pick up<br><span>where they left off.</span></h2>
                    <p>Some workflows need to wait for an external service before continuing. Define what happens when the response arrives. Fluxzero preserves progress and connects each response to the right process, even after a restart.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-interactions" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="PaymentProcess.java" label="Wait for a payment response" code={paymentProcessCode} />
                    <ProductCodePanel title="ConfirmReservation.java" label="Safe to repeat" code={confirmationCode} />
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="policy" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">07 · Access and privacy</p>
                    <h2 id="policy-title">You decide who may do what.<br><span>Fluxzero enforces it.</span></h2>
                    <p>Define the access rules that fit your product. Fluxzero enforces them before allowing a change. Information marked as private stays protected and can be erased without losing the surrounding history.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--stacked" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <div class="product-code-proof__code-stack">
                        <ProductCodePanel title="package-info.java" label="Secure by default" code={packagePolicyCode} />
                        <ProductCodePanel title="UpdateContactEmail.java" label="Ownership and protected data" code={personalDataCode} />
                    </div>
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>Identity supplied</dt><dd>Fluxzero gives your rule the authenticated customer making the change.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Access checked first</dt><dd>With sign-in required, Fluxzero rejects unauthenticated requests before the feature runs.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Private data stays erasable</dt><dd>Fluxzero stores protected values separately, so they can be erased while the surrounding history remains.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="web" aria-labelledby="web-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">08 · Reach in through the web</p>
                    <h2 id="web-title">Public web endpoints.<br><span>Private applications.</span></h2>
                    <p>Your web endpoints live in Fluxzero. Your application has no public endpoint of its own and securely pulls requests when it can handle them. This keeps it out of reach of direct network attacks. Excess traffic waits in Fluxzero instead of flooding the application.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--web" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="ReservationApi.java" label="Web request to command" code={webCode} />
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>Input checked</dt><dd>Fluxzero checks the submitted data against your requirements before running the feature.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Identity carried through</dt><dd>The feature receives the customer making the request without extra code to pass that identity along.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Response handled</dt><dd>Fluxzero sends the result back to the interface and turns errors into the appropriate web response.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="location-transparency" aria-labelledby="location-transparency-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">09 · Connect your features</p>
                    <h2 id="location-transparency-title">The same code.<br><span>Wherever the work runs.</span></h2>
                    <p>Send a request without choosing which application will handle it. Fluxzero delivers it and returns the result. Whether the handler runs in your own app or another one, the calling code stays the same.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--code" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="TicketApi.java" label="Call the query from 04" code={queryCallerCode} />
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="independent-consumers" aria-labelledby="independent-consumers-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">10 · Scale independently</p>
                    <h2 id="independent-consumers-title">Each part can scale<br><span>independently.</span></h2>
                    <p>Not every part of your application is equally busy. With separate consumers, parts run and scale independently. Fluxzero keeps their progress separate and distributes the work, so capacity can grow where it is needed.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--code" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="ReservationReceipts.java" label="A consumer with its own capacity" code={consumerCode} />
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section product-code-section" id="evolution" aria-labelledby="evolution-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">11 · Using the past</p>
                    <h2 id="evolution-title">New features can be built<br><span>from historical data.</span></h2>
                    <p>Fluxzero preserves your product’s history. Use it to add features retroactively, with the information as it was at the time. The same code processes earlier activity and continues with new activity.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="product-code-proof product-code-proof--history" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
                    <ProductCodePanel title="CustomerRewards.java" label="Event handler and complete history" code={historyCode} />
                    <dl class="product-code-proof__notes">
                        <div><dt>History supplied</dt><dd>Fluxzero feeds recorded activity to the new feature from the point you choose.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Earlier state reconstructed</dt><dd>Fluxzero supplies the data as it was then, without your code having to rebuild it.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Progress remembered</dt><dd>Fluxzero tracks how far the feature has processed and resumes after interruptions.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <section class="cloud-proof-next-conclusion product-code-conclusion" aria-labelledby="conclusion-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell" data-reveal>
                <p class="cloud-proof-next__eyebrow">The result</p>
                <h2 id="conclusion-title">Your product is<br><span>the entire application.</span></h2>
                <p>Your agent writes what the product should do. Fluxzero takes responsibility for making it run. What remains is an application entirely devoted to the product, from the first feature to a fully distributed system.</p>
                <div class="cloud-proof-next__actions">
                    <a class="v4-button v4-button--primary" href="/get-started"><span>Start building</span><i class="bx bx-right-arrow-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                    <a class="v4-button v4-button--secondary" href="/docs"><span>Inspect the SDK</span><i class="bx bx-right-arrow-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <MarketingFooter />
    <script src="/js/v4.js?v=20260904-3" defer></script>
    <script src="/js/product-code.js?v=20260911-2" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
